{"archetypes":[{"name":"publish-lifecycle","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Diff threads PUBLISH_OK, SESSION_ID, SUMMARY_OUTCOME, and step sentinels across several bash entrypoints.","prompt_body":"Investigate the /design publish lifecycle state machine across design-publish.sh, design-log-publish.sh, design-pause-save.sh, render-final-summary.sh, render-run-summary.sh, and SKILL.md. Check whether nonzero publish exits, contradictory PUBLISH_OK envelopes, empty SESSION_ID, failed-publish, publish-skipped, rename gates, reentry markers, and step-5c sentinel writes all transition consistently. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"repo-boundary","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Diff adds OWNER/REPO validation and forwarding near gh calls and source-env boundaries.","prompt_body":"Examine every new or changed --repo handling path for validation order, argv precedence, gh argument construction, and fallback to hub defaults. Pay special attention to source-env.sh adoption, current-design-env persistence, direct script invocation, and pause-check call sites that could retarget GitHub reads or writes. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pause-recovery","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Pause/resume recovery now distinguishes fail-closed publish errors from recoverable recovery-branch publish failures.","prompt_body":"Review the pause/resume recovery flow in design-pause-save.sh, design-postplan-emit.sh, SKILL.md, and the related tests. Verify that recoverable publish failures with RECOVERY_BRANCH still produce resumable markers while contradictory or malformed cases cannot write successful pause state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"summary-contracts","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Diff changes shared render contracts for publish-skipped, failed-publish, fallback summaries, and run-log path synthesis.","prompt_body":"Trace the summary rendering contract between render-final-summary.sh and the shared render-run-summary.sh for design outcomes. Check primary and degraded fallback output semantics for publish-skipped and failed-publish, especially Outcome bullets, Run logs N/A behavior, recovery prose suppression, and impacts on other skill call sites. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
